studio/take.py, studio/takes.py, studio/render_worker.py  One take -> a week (libraries and programs, called; no code copied)
  The video worker (GitHub Actions take.yml, or a self-hosted machine; requirements-worker.txt) uses, as libraries:
  - faster-whisper  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
      Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 SYSTRAN. Speech-to-text with word timestamps (`small` model, CPU int8).
  - Whisper model weights (CTranslate2 conversion "Systran/faster-whisper-small")  https://github.com/openai/whisper
      Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI. Downloaded at run time, not redistributed.
  - Silero VAD (the voice activity model bundled inside faster-whisper)  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
      Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team. Skips silence before transcription.
  - PySceneDetect  https://github.com/Breakthrough/PySceneDetect
      Licence: BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (C) 2014, Brandon Castellano. Scene cuts (ContentDetector) to split shots
      and snap clip edges.
  - MediaPipe (Tasks Face Detector) and the BlazeFace short-range model  https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe
      Licence: Apache License 2.0, Copyright The MediaPipe Authors. The model file is downloaded at run time from
      storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models; not redistributed. Used for the 9:16 face-tracked reframe.
  - FFmpeg with libass and libx264  https://ffmpeg.org  (LGPL-2.1+, GPL-2.0+ when built with GPL parts such as x264)
      Invoked as a separate executable (subprocess) for cutting, cropping, burning in ASS captions and encoding;
      not linked or bundled. Source: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
  The caption styling (ASS with libass), the moment scorer, the crop smoothing, the cover renderer and the slot
  planner are our own code.

